# Cline Rules for AutoMakeClip

## Default workflow
- Start every task by inspecting relevant files first.
- Do not guess project structure.
- Read README, package.json, config files, and relevant source files before editing.
- Explain the plan before editing.
- Mention the exact files you plan to change.

## Commands
- Run commands one at a time.
- Before each command, explain what it does and why it is safe.
- After a failed command, stop and explain the error before trying another command.
- Do not install packages unless you explain why and ask first.

## Never run without explicit user approval
- rm -rf
- del /s
- rmdir /s
- Remove-Item -Recurse
- git reset --hard
- git clean -fd
- npm uninstall
- database reset commands
- format/shutdown/restart commands
- global installs

## Smoke testing
- After edits, run the smallest relevant smoke test.
- Inspect package.json scripts first.
- Prefer npm run build, npm test, or npm run lint if available.
- Do not run npm run dev unless needed.

## Coding behavior
- Make minimal changes.
- Do not rewrite unrelated files.
- Do not invent APIs.
- Follow existing imports and patterns.
- If unsure, say what you are unsure about.
